+=head2 Problems loading XRC on Linux
+
+Linux builds retain the declared wxWidgets libraries as direct shared-library
+dependencies. This lets the extension's RUNPATH locate libraries installed
+by Alien::wxWidgets, including libraries used only by another wxWidgets
+library. With the linker's C<--as-needed> default, XRC's HTML and advanced
+libraries can otherwise be discarded from the extension's dependency list.
+
+After changing linker flags, run C<perl Makefile.PL> and C<make> again to
+relink the extensions. Use C<make test> with a working graphical display.
+Plugin load failures return failure to the caller instead of dereferencing
+a null library handle.
+
